@@ -27405,7 +27405,7 @@ msgstr ""
 #. Hades: help of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvsdrtarget"; translated in Estuary (#52611)
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 msgctxt "#61131"
-msgid "On a display that takes no HDR, an HDR video is converted to ordinary SDR (Dolby Vision always; HDR10, HDR10+ and HLG with the tone mapping method \"Reference (BT.2390)\", the default, or \"BT.2390, libplacebo's knee\"), and this says what kind of display that SDR is made for. Reference (the default): a display that shows white at 203 cd/m² with gamma 2.4, as the standards define for SDR made from HDR. Bright room: a display set brighter, white at 300 cd/m² with gamma 2.2, as many TVs in a lit living room: choose it if the picture looks too bright or washed out with Reference. Projector: a dimmer display, white at 100 cd/m²: choose it if the picture looks too dark with Reference. Custom: the white and the gamma that you set below. Nothing is clipped in any of them: what is brighter than the display's white is compressed. Applies from the next video."
+msgid "On a display that takes no HDR, an HDR video is converted to ordinary SDR (Dolby Vision always; HDR10, HDR10+ and HLG with the tone mapping method \"Reference (BT.2390)\", the default, or \"BT.2390, libplacebo's knee\"), and this says what kind of display that SDR is made for. Reference (the default): a display that shows white at 203 cd/m² with gamma 2.4, as the standards define for SDR made from HDR. Bright room: a display set brighter, white at 300 cd/m² with gamma 2.2, as many TVs in a lit living room: choose it if the picture looks too bright or washed out with Reference. Projector: a dimmer display, white at 100 cd/m²: choose it if the picture looks too dark with Reference. Custom: the white and the gamma that you set below. Nothing is clipped in any of them: what is brighter than the display's white is compressed. Applies from the next video. Up to 1.1 it was in the Dolby Vision group."
 msgstr ""
 
 #. Hades: value of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvsdrtarget": reference
@@ -28228,7 +28228,7 @@ msgstr ""
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 #. Hades: help of Kodi's setting "winsystem.ishdrdisplay" (Adjust display HDR mode, System > Display, in place of Kodi's #36299): what Off does in Hades; translated in Estuary (#54502)
 msgctxt "#62502"
-msgid "Lets the display switch to its HDR mode for HDR videos. On (the default): HDR10, HDR10+ and HLG videos go out as HDR, and the display shows them in its HDR mode. Off: the display stays in SDR, and those videos are converted to SDR, as for a display without HDR (see \"HDR to SDR: the display it is made for\"). Dolby Vision videos, and the videos that a setting sends as Dolby Vision, still go out as Dolby Vision while \"Native Dolby Vision output\" is on: to have them as SDR too, turn that off as well, or, for one video, choose \"As SDR (without HDR)\" for it while it plays, in \"Output of this video\" of the player information (the O key of a keyboard, Info on a remote, then OK on that button). To send only HLG videos as SDR, leave this on and use \"Play HDR videos as SDR\", below. Applies from the next video."
+msgid "Lets the display switch to its HDR mode for HDR videos. On (the default): HDR10, HDR10+ and HLG videos go out as HDR, and the display shows them in its HDR mode. Off: the display stays in SDR, and those videos are converted to SDR, as for a display without HDR (see \"HDR to SDR: the display it is made for\"). Dolby Vision videos, and the videos that a setting sends as Dolby Vision, still go out as Dolby Vision while \"Native Dolby Vision output\" is on: to have them as SDR too, turn that off as well, or, for one video, choose \"As SDR (without HDR)\" for it while it plays, in \"Output of this video\" of the player information (the O key of a keyboard, Info on a remote, then OK on that button). To send only HLG videos as SDR, leave this on and use \"Play HDR videos as SDR\", below. Applies from the next video. Up to 1.1 this setting was in Player > Videos."
 msgstr ""
 
